[[Tesla, Inc.]] is an [[electric vehicle]] manufacturer and [[clean energy]] company founded in [[San Carlos, California]] in 2003 by American entrepreneurs [[Martin Eberhard]] and [[Marc Tarpenning]]. The company is named after Serbian-American inventor [[Nikola Tesla]]. Tesla is the world's leading electric vehicle manufacturer by market cap.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Largest automakers by market capitalization |url=https://companiesmarketcap.com/automakers/largest-automakers-by-market-cap/ |access-date=2025-07-19 |website=companiesmarketcap.com |language=en-US}}</ref> As of 2023, Tesla's global vehicle sales were 1.77 million units annually, the 14th-highest total among auto manufacturers worldwide.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Worldwide Car Sales {{!}} Top-Selling Manufacturers 2023 & 2024 |url=https://roadgenius.com/cars/statistics/sales-by-manufacturer/ |access-date=2025-07-19 |website=Road Genius |language=en-US}}</ref>

