{{Short description|Science that understands human crowds}}
'''Social physics''' or '''sociophysics''' is an interdisciplinary field of science which uses mathematical tools inspired by [[physics]] to understand the behavior of human crowds. In a modern commercial use, it can also refer to the analysis of social phenomena with [[big data]].

Social physics is closely related to [[econophysics]], which uses physics methods to describe [[economics]].<ref>{{cite arXiv|title=Social Thermodynamics 2.0 |last=Tsekov|first=Roumen| date=2023 |class=physics.soc-ph |eprint=2307.05984}}</ref>

